*.pyc
__pycache__/
third-party-engines/*

# Generated from a run's metrics by plot.py; the .jsonl beside it is the record worth keeping.
runs/*.html

# A tee of a run's console output, kept only so a live run can be tailed. Everything in it that
# matters is already in the .jsonl, in a form something can read.
runs/*.log

# Connect 4 checkpoints. The tic-tac-toe one is committed because it is near-perfect and 25KB;
# these are 5MB apiece with their optimiser state and, so far, only evidence that the curve rises.
models/connect4*.pt

# Except a long run's resume point, which is committed as it goes precisely so that losing the
# machine costs a few generations rather than the run. See `zero.py train --commit-every`.
!models/connect4-latest.pt

# One-off experiment runners. The findings get written down; the scratch does not need to live
# at the repo root. Their metrics under runs/ are kept, being the evidence behind the findings.
_*.py
